Package: workmux
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, git
Recommends: tmux
Description: git worktrees and tmux windows for parallel development
 workmux is an opinionated workflow tool that orchestrates git worktrees and
 tmux windows as isolated development environments, so several features (or
 several AI coding agents) can be worked on in parallel without stashing,
 branch switching or conflicts.
 .
 A single command creates a worktree with a matching tmux window, copies or
 symlinks the files a fresh checkout is missing, runs the install commands and
 starts the agent; another one merges the branch and tears the whole thing down
 again. It also provides a TUI dashboard and a tmux sidebar for monitoring
 agent status across worktrees.
 .
 tmux is the default backend; kitty, WezTerm and Zellij are also supported,
 which is why tmux is recommended rather than required.
